Give the product tree the tokens the widget vocabulary needs

The five components the vision critique asked for cannot be wired into this
tree, because the tokens they speak do not exist here. Thirteen --ns-* names
were missing, all of them semantic rather than presentational:

  --ns-series-1..6   the fixed chart cycle (H3). A series keeps its colour
                     across renders and across routes because the cycle is
                     keyed by index, never by data order.
  --ns-chart-grid    faint dashed gridlines (H6)
  --ns-chart-axis    axis ticks, sitting outside the bounded plot
  --ns-absent        the tone a movement or amount takes when it was never
                     measured (M1) — never a zero, never the muted grey
  --ns-tip-bg/fg     the chart's pointer bubble, which inverts against the
                     card in both themes so no component asks which theme is
                     active (T3)
  --ns-radius-3xl    24px, the containing card's radius (C7)
  --ns-shadow-ambient  the diffuse multi-stop elevation a card carries (C8)

Every one is declared in both themes where it is theme-variant. The series
cycle keeps its light-mode order in dark and only changes ramp step, so a
series survives a theme switch as the same series; paper-7 for series-6 is
deliberately the identical step in both, because it is the neutral slot.

tokens.json and the generated tokens.css are edited together, as T1 requires.
Parity checked programmatically: 188 declared in JSON, 188 defined in CSS, no
divergence in either direction.

Values are taken from design/ledgerline-ui rather than invented here, so this
tree and the design tree do not drift.
EOF
