[0m$ [0mcd /home/agent/projects/netscript/wave7-billing-steer2 && git add -A && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'
Stop counting Ledgerline's own components as upstream registry items

The gallery's headline number was a lie. `registryMeta.total` read 72 while
`@netscript/fresh-ui` publishes 66 — the six components this product owns
(status-badge, money-text, run-state-stepper, exception-badge, transition-feed,
provisional-tag) had been folded into `registryCatalog` and counted as though
`ui:add` would install them. It would not: they exist because Ledgerline
exists.

R3 is explicit about this. Ledgerline's components now live in their own
`ledgerlineCatalog` with their own `ledgerlineMeta`, and `registryMeta.total`
is back to a fact about the upstream package. The gallery renders both: a
"Ledgerline widgets" section leads, and the upstream sections stay upstream.

The `ledgerline-product` collection is dropped with the move — it referenced
names that are no longer in `registryCatalog`, so it could only have gone
stale. Nothing else in the app reads `registryCollections`; only the gallery
consumes the registry.

This is the seam the five incoming components register into, so it lands
before them rather than after: each one should be able to add exactly one
catalogue entry and one demo without moving anything else.
EOF
