[0m$ [0mcd /home/agent/projects/netscript/wave7-billing-steer2 && git status --short && git add -A && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'
Add WidgetCard — the one five-band card grammar

The critic's ranked item 3, and the container the other four compose into, so
it lands before them.

Every reference card obeys one anatomy — header (glyph + title left, one pill
action right) · range control · hero metric + delta chip · body visualisation ·
footer columns or a full-width CTA — and none of Ledgerline's surfaces did.
`.ns-card__header` is hardcoded `flex-direction: column` for a title plus a
description paragraph, which leaves no slot for a leading glyph, no
right-pinned action, and no inline hero band. The result is a page of
rectangular tiles that each improvise.

The header is restored to a row here rather than forked into a second card:
this file is imported after `card.css` and `surface-styles.css`, so it rides
the `class` seam the base component already merges (T4).

Radius encodes containment, so it is not uniform (C7). The card is the largest
radius on the page (`--ns-radius-3xl`, 24px, with the new diffuse
`--ns-shadow-ambient`), a panel inside it steps down to `--ns-radius-xl`, and
every control, chip and segmented cell inside those is a full pill.

Two decisions worth flagging:

· The hero's size lives on the band, not on the amount component. Any amount
  dropped into band three becomes the card's answer, so a caller does not
  repeat a size prop at every call site, and the figure is ~3x the title above
  it instead of the same size (C2).
· The hero does not take the direction colour (M9). `MoneyText` colours by
  sign, but a hero states a balance, not a movement — in the reference cards
  the hero number is plain and only the delta beside it is green. Colouring a
  figure green *because it is positive* is precisely the failure M9 names, so
  the band overrides it and the DeltaChip on the same baseline carries
  direction.

Registered in `ledgerlineCatalog` with two demos: the full five-band card, and
the same card with no range, no hero and no footer, because a card with no
single answer to give has no hero.
EOF
