[0m$ [0mcd /home/agent/projects/netscript/wave7-billing-steer2 && git status --short && git add -A && git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'
Add SemicircularGauge — the 180° two-tone run-progress arc

The critic's ranked item 5, first half. `Donut` could only draw a 360° circle
with a vertical legend list; the reference's hero widget is a 180° two-tone
gauge with a centre readout, and there was no way to render one.

Two things are load-bearing, and the 360° donut got both wrong:

· `stroke-linecap="butt"` (H8). A round cap bulges past the terminal it is
  supposed to end at, drops below the baseline, and bleeds across the junction
  between two segments. The reference terminates with flat horizontal cuts
  flush with the baseline, and the junction between the two colours is a crisp
  radial cut with no gap.
· The centre block is absolutely positioned against the plot's *height*, so it
  stays centred inside the arc at every width rather than at one breakpoint.

Geometry is hand-authored SVG (H1) — no charting library — and colour comes
from the fixed `--ns-series-1..6` cycle keyed by index, so a series keeps its
identity across renders and across routes and a sort cannot re-colour it (H3).

`value` on a segment is geometry and is never rendered; the amount the reader
sees arrives as a preformatted `display` string (H2). The gauge formats
nothing.

`total` is the denominator — every item the run covers, including the ones no
segment accounts for — so the unallocated remainder stays visible as track
rather than being absorbed. `total={null}` means the total was not measured,
which renders a labelled empty frame: "this run has not been computed yet" is a
different statement from "0 of 412" and the chart must not conflate them (H7,
M1).

Registered in `ledgerlineCatalog` with the populated run — 318 issued and 47
in review of 412 items — beside the empty frame, because a widget that has
never been seen without data has not been designed (D4).
EOF
